Instructions for inverting the video feed.
Use this set of instructions if your video is upside down because of the way you mounted the camera

Find this code in the camera.__init__ section

config = self.camera.create_video_configuration(
    main={"size": (640, 480)},
    controls={"FrameRate": 30}
)

Change it to this:

from libcamera import Transform

config = self.camera.create_video_configuration(
    main={"size": (640, 480)},
    controls={"FrameRate": 30},
    transform=Transform(hflip=1, vflip=1)
)

Explanation:
vflip=1 flips vertically, hflip=1 flips horizontally. Both together gives you a 180° rotation,
which is what you need when the camera is mounted upside down. If the image is mirrored but
the right way up, use just vflip=1 on its own.

The Transform import needs to go at the top of the file with the other imports, or you can put
it inline just above the config line — either works.
